WEBVTT

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:06.463
As a leader of non-exempt employees, your review is what keeps timecards accurate.

00:00:07.813 --> 00:00:13.211
Make sure your team completes this training, and knows the program, the resources, and the process.

00:00:14.561 --> 00:00:23.625
Timecards with overtime or on-call hours reach you on Thursday at 9:00 PM Pacific, with a notification in Workday and by email.

00:00:23.625 --> 00:00:27.979
Timecards with only regular hours are approved automatically.

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:31.037
Even so, review regularly.

00:00:31.037 --> 00:00:36.028
Make it a ritual, and validate that your team's reported hours are accurate.

00:00:37.378 --> 00:00:40.684
If something is wrong, do not use Send Back in Workday.

00:00:40.684 --> 00:00:42.848
Talk with your team member directly.

00:00:42.848 --> 00:00:46.935
A conversation makes the correction clear, and builds better habits.

00:00:48.285 --> 00:00:55.178
Workday also alerts you when a part-time employee or intern has not entered time, or when records overlap.

00:00:55.178 --> 00:00:56.413
Follow up promptly.

00:00:57.763 --> 00:01:03.630
Encourage your team to take their required rest and meal breaks, and talk about schedules in your one-to-ones.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:12.852
Make sure a delegate is always assigned to approve on your behalf, especially during time off, unscheduled absences, or leave.

00:01:14.202 --> 00:01:17.707
Your final deadline is Sunday at 6:30 PM Pacific.

00:01:17.707 --> 00:01:22.714
After that, anything unapproved is processed for payment as it stands.
